   "evidence": "Lines 236-238: `let K : DisKinematics V := { p := P, pPrime := a \u2022 L.nPlus + c \u2022 L.nMinus + s \u2022 e, k := 0, kPrime := 0, q := 0, hq := by simp }`; the subsequent proof uses only `hKp`, `hKm`, `hKT` and `tMom_eq_tMin_add`, none of which mention `k`, `kPrime`, `q`. `DisKinematics` fixes `q = k - kPrime` (Kinematics/Basic.lean:62-64), so arbitrary lepton momenta are admissible at no proof cost.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Kinematics/MomentumTransferBound.lean",
   "fix": "Take `k kPrime : V` as parameters and build the witness with `q := k - kPrime`, `hq := rfl`, adding `K.k = k \u2227 K.kPrime = kPrime` to the conclusion (or state the core fact at the momentum level, `\u2203 P', g P' P' = MY ^ 2 \u2227 L.plus (P - P') = \u03be * L.plus P \u2227 g (P - P') (P - P') = t`, and derive the `DisKinematics` form). The proof is unchanged. Then drop the `Q\u00b2 = 0` caveats from both docstrings; `setOf_tMom_eq_Iic_tMin` (line 271) inherits the same caveat from this witness and its docstring note at lines 268-270 can be narrowed accordingly.",
   "issue": "`exists_tMom_eq_of_le_tMin` builds its witness with `k := 0, kPrime := 0, q := 0`, although the proof touches only `p` and `pPrime` (`tMom`, `MY2`, `xiLC` are functions of `P`, `P'` alone \u2014 cf. `tMom_congr`/`MX2_congr` in Diffractive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:249-263). The lepton data is unconstrained input, not something the theorem determines, so fixing it to zero is a gratuitous specialization: it forces `Q\u00b2 = 0`, which is the caveat the docstring (lines 215-217) and the module docstring (lines 37-41) have to carry, and it makes the lemma unusable for the non-emptiness milestone the PR description says it supplies the configuration for.",
